  "notes": "A hybrid compound of {自己|じこ} (self) and ＰＲ (public relations, from English). Despite using 'PR,' this term specifically means presenting oneself positively, not public relations in the corporate sense.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {自己|じこ}ＰＲ{欄|らん} — self-promotion section (on a resume or application form)\n- {自己|じこ}ＰＲを{書|か}く — to write a self-introduction\n- {自己|じこ}ＰＲが{上手|じょうず} — to be good at self-promotion\n- {自己|じこ}ＰＲのポイント — key points of self-promotion\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nA critical component of the Japanese job-hunting ({就活|しゅうかつ}) process. Students and job seekers spend considerable time crafting their {自己|じこ}ＰＲ, which is expected in resumes ({履歴書|りれきしょ}) and interviews. It typically covers one's strengths, experiences, and what one can contribute to the company.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {自己紹介|じこしょうかい}: self-introduction — a broader term for introducing oneself in any context, not limited to selling one's strengths",
